{"name":"Coal Mine","hex":"#220033","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"coal mine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mine from which coal (such as lignite or anthracite) is mined."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coal_mine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coal mining","blocks":[{"text":"Coal mining is the process of extracting coal from the ground or from a mine. Coal is valued for its energy content and since the 1880s has been widely used to generate electricity. In the United Kingdom and South Africa, a coal mine and its structures are a colliery, a coal mine is called a \"pit\", and above-ground mining structures are referred to as a \"pit head\". In Australia, \"colliery\" generally refers to an underground coal mine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Coal_mine_Wyoming.jpg/330px-Coal_mine_Wyoming.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coal_mining"},{"title":"Coal","blocks":[{"text":"Coal is a combustible black or brownish-black sedimentary rock, formed as layers called coal seams. Coal is mostly carbon with variable amounts of other elements, chiefly hydrogen, sulfur, oxygen, and nitrogen. It is a fossil fuel, formed when plants decay into peat which is converted into coal by the heat and pressure of deep burial over millions of years. Vast deposits formed from wetlands called coal forests that covered much of the tropics during the late Carboniferous and early Permian."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Bituminous_Coal.JPG/330px-Bituminous_Coal.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coal"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Lackawanna_Coal_Mine_car%2C_Nov_2014.jpg/500px-Lackawanna_Coal_Mine_car%2C_Nov_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conten